A||N||7||Fleabitdog||Wheel bearing for 88?||||13||
Z||000000||Fleabitdog||09-03-2000||03:56 PM||||Has anybody needed a wheel bearing for an 88 lately? I have talked with Delco and they discontinued thiers but they told me to contact BCA Bearings. I did and they have also discontinued thiers. I have not been able to locate a replacement. Does anybody know where I can get one? I have been told that the bearing and hub is a pressed assembly but with an arbor press you can do it just replace the bearing. Thanks  Dog||||reg||13
Z||000001||88formula||09-03-2000||06:47 PM||||I did for the rear of my formula. I bought Timken bearings for the rear and paid $50 each at Autopalace here in Worcester Massachusetts. The Fiero Store also sells them but they cost more.<P>I think they are the same as the 84-87 year bearings, which are not pressed in.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 09-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||09-04-2000||10:31 PM||||If you are looking for a front wheel bearing/hub assembly, I bought mine at Advance Auto parts. It <I>wasn't</I> cheap. Got it about 5-6 months ago. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||09-05-2000||02:25 AM||||I had a shot rear bearing on my '88 Coupe a short time ago. I replaced the whole hub assy. and got it at a NAPA store. I only paid $60.00 but I also got it at a good discount. Actually I was under the impression that you have to replace the whole assy.(??)<P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||09-05-2000||03:14 AM||||Ozzy, do you like to move around!!  Australia to somewhere US. to Washington state to Idaho?? all within a year or so!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||09-05-2000||08:41 PM||||I bought a new Timken front wheel bearing assembly for my 88 Formula (now sold) last year for about $95 from my local AutoZone store.  I believe the rear wheel bearing assemblies are the same in the all 85-88 Fieros and run about 1/2 that price.||||reg||1
Z||000006||triksterut||09-06-2000||11:31 AM||||You can use an later model Pontiac 6000 wheel bearings.  They are exactly the same and cheaper.  And I do not believe they have been discontinued...yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jeremy||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ozzy||09-06-2000||12:04 PM||||Sure seems that way RossT. Actually I moved to the U.S. from Australia about 10 yrs ago. <P>In actual fact, in the last 18 months my wife and I have lived in Oregon, Washington, Utah and Idaho. And if this job I've been chasing forever come thru...we'll be moving back to California where we started. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And I HATE moving!<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
